  "intro_html": "<p>The normal approach to the Geltenhütte always follows the water - in order to savour the journey, a start at the tranquil Lauenen is always worthwhile. From there, you must first pass the \"Rohr\"; damp flower filled meadows, then cross the floodplain and young forest of the Louwibach. After short steeper section you will reach the Lauenensee - chance for a bath and a bite to eat. After that, the well built mountain path always traces the water's edge, until it surprisingly evades the impressive \"Gälteschutz\" waterfall. Now it is not far to the Geltenhütte, where further water wonders are to be discovered.</p>",
